xnu 0220: the kernel can install the CoreAnimation dylibs at boot

A userland change is one file, but getting it into the phone has been a 16 GiB
userdata flash: the iOS root is HFS+, the host cannot mount it, and the only
write path is a partition image. The kernel can carry the dylibs instead -- it
already carries the GPU and touch firmware -- and write them into
/private/var/vm, which is the writable copy the injector prefers over
/usr/libexec.

Boot argument glblob=1. The blobs are tools/gen-glblob.py's output, generated
into bsd/dev at build time and never committed, so a kernel built without them
(for instance in CI) simply does not take this path.
--- a/bsd/dev/mondrian_ufs.c
+++ b/bsd/dev/mondrian_ufs.c
@@ -44,6 +44,9 @@
